# SlayZone Env Vars — Standalone Hub & Runner

Deployment-relevant vars for standalone (non-supervised) hub + runner, plus every var surfaced by the full 4-cluster deep-dive. Dev/build/e2e/internal vars summarized at bottom.

**Precedence everywhere:** `env var > SLAYZONE_RUNNER_CONFIG file (runner) > ~/.slayzone/config.json > generated/default`

**CWD-anchoring = default-only, NO new knob.** Standalone (non-supervised) hub/runner default `SLAYZONE_HOME_DIR` + `SLAYZONE_STORE_DIR` + `SLAYZONE_RUNNER_CREDENTIALS_DIR` to CWD. "Relocate everything" = launch from another dir (`cd /srv/slayzone && slayzone-hub`) — no env var. Fine-grained overrides stay for the niche "config here, DB there" split.

**Minimize legend** (does the operator hold info the process can't derive at boot?):
- 🟢 **keep** — genuinely operator-only info
- 🔵 **derive** — process can compute it; keep only as optional override
- 🟠 **hide** — subsumed by a richer input; code stays, drop from docs
- 🔴 **delete** — derivable/dup/dead/redundant; remove the knob entirely

